cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this process, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-rfc-skill: an RFC process for human-LLM co-authored software specifications"
authors:
  - family-names: "Nunley"
    given-names: "Norman"
    email: "nnunley@gmail.com"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nnunley/llm-rfc-skill"
license: "CC-BY-4.0 AND MIT AND CC0-1.0"
abstract: >-
  A specification-authoring process for one or more humans collaborating
  with one or more LLM agents: an IETF-derived RFC lifecycle with literate,
  machine-verifiable evidence and a cumulative conformance corpus. Designed
  and formalized by Norman Nunley, Jr in collaboration with Claude
  (Anthropic), 2026.
